      "claim": "In horticultural contexts, \"looking their best\" for hostas refers to the expression of their ornamental foliage traits (color, variegation, texture), not merely physiological health.",
      "evidence": "Garden award criteria (e.g., All-America Selections) and nursery marketing emphasize leaf color patterns and variegation as the primary qualities judged for hostas.",
